{
  "description": "Stripped renditions (SOM §11.10; reading_view part *Stripped renditions and the merge back*). `cases`: stripNotationText(text, options) for one value — `expect` holds the stripped text, the counts per kind, the review marks that went inside a dropped element, the appendix entries (numbered from 1), the pieces (anchor in the stripped text, origin in the input, removed and inserted text, labels) and the codes of the error findings a refused value has. Applying every piece at its anchor gives the input back. A case whose drop list is only `comments` also equals stripAnnotationsText(text). `usageCases`: SpecStripOptions.fromNames — the expanded lists, or the usage error's message. `headerCases`: SpecReadableHeader.parse(line) — the switches, the source and format() of the parse, or null. `documentCases`: SpecDocumentStrip.strip over the corpus model (and docspecs_schema.yaml) unless `model` is false — the stripped document, the values the emptying rule kept, the list items removed, the appendix, the counts, the readable header, the `.readable.md` (null without a model) and the kinds of the validity findings.",
